    "continent": "Oceania",
    "notes_unique": "Battle of Peleliu (September-November 1944, US Marines vs Japanese, 2 months, 10,695 US casualties including 1,794 dead, ~11,000 Japanese killed of 11,000, one of bloodiest Pacific battles, Bloody Nose Ridge, coral caves, questionable strategic necessity); Nuclear-free constitution (1979, world's first nuclear-free constitution, required 75% referendum to override, 7 referendums failed before amendment allowed COFA with US nuclear transit, delayed independence by 15 years); Palau National Marine Sanctuary (2015, 80% of EEZ protected, 500,000 km² no-take zone, one of world's largest, marine conservation leader); Rock Islands Southern Lagoon (UNESCO World Heritage, 445 uninhabited limestone islands, Jellyfish Lake/Ongeim'l Tketau with millions of golden jellyfish that lost stingers through evolution, unique); matrilineal society (women control land/clan resources, clan mothers choose chiefs, women central to political decisions, bul system of conservation, unique in Micronesia); Babeldaob (largest island, megalithic terraces/earthworks among largest ancient structures in Pacific, pre-European, purpose debated); Japanese legacy (1914-44, Koror developed as administrative centre, Japanese population outnumbered Palauans 4:1 by 1940, cultural influences persist: food/bento, words, infrastructure, Shinto shrines remnants); Compact of Free Association (COFA, 1994 last Trust Territory, renewed, US military access, citizens can live in US); diving (world-class, Blue Corner, German Channel, shipwrecks, manta rays); small population (18k, one of smallest UN member states); storyboards (bai house carved panels depicting legends, valuable art form); bul (traditional moratorium on fishing areas, indigenous conservation, inspired modern marine policies)",
